        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Lands Bunnanertish, Knockanillaun, Ballina, Co. Mayo \r\n\r\nc. 2.90ha - c. 7.16 acres \r\n\r\nFor Sale by Live Virtual Online & Public Auction\r\n\r\nWednesday 14th of October 2026 \r\n\r\nAt\r\n\r\nWilsons Auctions, Kingswood Interchange, Naas Road, Dublin 22\r\n\r\nExcellent Potential \r\n\r\nLocation Ballina 7km, Crossmolina 7km, Enniscrone 20km, Castlebar 39km, Sligo 66km. \r\n\r\nThe lands are located on the L51549, accessed from the N59, 7km west of the historic market town of Ballina. Population (2022) 10,556. Ballina is a town in north Co Mayo It lies at the mouth of the River Moy near Killala Bay, with the Ox Mountains to the east and the Nephin Mountains to the west. Ballina railway station is located on the N26 beside the bus station, with trains going to Castlebar, Westport or Dublin. The town provides excellent choice of highly regarded primary schools and established secondary institutions, modern Ballina Athletic Track, sporting clubs, a vibrant town centre full of artisan cafés, boutique shopping, and modern sports facilities, Ballina provides an idyllic setting for a balanced and active lifestyle.\" The famed surfing beach at Enniscrone is a short drive. \r\n\r\nDescription Folio MY59043F\r\n\r\nThe lands are contained within folio MY59043F and amount to c. 2.90ha - c. 7.16 acres. The subject lands are in one irregular shaped block. The lands are laid out in large open plan manageable divisions, with mature boundaries of hedging trees. The lands currently in grass are good quality suited to livestock and most farming enterprises. Near the road is an older type detached shed. Good road frontage. \r\n\r\nIdeal location for a one-off house, subject to the necessary planning. \r\n\r\nThe lands are being sold as seen and not subject to planning. \r\n\r\nCoordinates 54.133668, -9.232424\r\n\r\nViewing By Appointment Only\r\n\r\nSolicitor Iseult Cody, Beauchamps, Sir John Rogerson's Quay, \r\n\r\nVAT Refer to legal contracts."
